<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.15.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01129</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.15.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f60d1e09-c2d3-4540-9c1e-c5d864df6e73</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para><emphasis><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Here are the first two terms of a geometric sequence: 2, 4. What is the 5th term in the sequence?
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>32</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    What are the common ratios of each geometric sequence? 
  </item>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      1, 1, 1, 1</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      256, 128, 64
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer</emphasis><emphasis>: </emphasis>0.5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      18, 54, 162
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      0.8, 0.08, 0.008
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0.1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      0.008, 0.08, 0.8
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>10</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>A person owes $1,000 on a credit card that charges an interest rate of 2% per month.</item>
</list>
<para>Complete this table showing the credit card balance each month if they do not make any payments. Enter each answer to the hundredths place.</para>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Month</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Total Bill In Dollars</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
       1,000
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1,020
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1,040.40
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       4
      </entry>
      <entry>a.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        5
      </entry>
      <entry>b.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        6
      </entry>
      <entry>c.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        7
      </entry>
      <entry>d.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        8
      </entry>
      <entry>e.
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      Month 4
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1061.21</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      Month 5
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1082.43</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      Month 6
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1104.08</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      Month 7
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1126.16</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      Month 8
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1148.68</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>A Sierpinski triangle can be created by starting with an equilateral triangle, breaking the triangle into 4 congruent equilateral triangles, and then removing the middle triangle. Starting from a single black equilateral triangle with an area of 256 square inches, here are the first four steps:</item>
</list>
<para><figure><media alt="A pattern of 4 congruent equilateral triangles. Starting with the first triangle, remove smaller congruent triangles to create the triangle to its right."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/846475c330baf5f005af08f87b151ae7cc7e047f"/></media></figure></para>
<para>Complete this table showing the number of shaded triangles in each step and the area of each triangle. Enter each answer as an integer.</para>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Step Number</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number Of Shaded Triangles</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Area Of One Shaded Triangle In Square Inches</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
       0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        256
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       1
      </entry>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        a.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
       b.
      </entry>
      <entry>
        c.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
        d.
      </entry>
      <entry>
       e.
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        4
      </entry>
      <entry>
       f.
      </entry>
      <entry>
       g.
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 1, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>64; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 64.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 2, what is the number of shaded triangles?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 9; The number of shaded triangles is 9.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 2, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 16; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 16.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 3, what is the number of shaded triangles?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>27; The number of shaded triangles is 27.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 3, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>4; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 4.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 4, what is the number of shaded triangles?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>81; The number of shaded triangles is 81.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      In Step 4, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches?
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 1.</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>For each geometric sequence with missing terms, find the common ratio that might help determine the missing terms.
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="1" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, 5, 25, ___, 625

    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item>–1, ___, –36, 216, ___
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –6</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      10, 5, ___, ___, 0.625
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>0.5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, ___, 36, –108, ___
      
    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> –3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item>
      ___, 12, 18, 27, ___

    </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1.5</para></section>
